respiratory illness in primary school children in Kuala Lumpur</article-title><source>Int J Epidemiol</source><volume>20</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>144</fpage><lpage>150</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2066213</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bener</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Jawadi</surname><given-names>TQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozkaragoz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Frayh</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Gomes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993a</year><article-title>Bronchial asthma and wheeze in a desert country</article-title><source>Indian J Pediatr</source><volume>60</volume><fpage>791</fpage><lpage>797</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8200703</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bener</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Jawadi</surname><given-names>TQ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozkaragoz</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Anderson</surname><given-names>JAD</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993b</year><article-title>Prevalence of asthma and wheeze in two different climatic areas of Saudi Arabia</article-title><source>Indian J Chest Dis Allied Sci</source><volume>35</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8225434</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bener</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Facharzt</surname><given-names>ARAF</given-names></name><name><surname>Al-Jawadi</surname><given-names>TQ</given-names></name></person-group><year>1991</year><article-title>Parental smoking and the risk of childhood asthma</article-title><source>J Asthma</source><volume>28</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>281</fpage><lpage>286</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1890081</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bergmann</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Edenharter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergmann</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Forster</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bauer</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name><name><surname>Wahn</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Atopic dermatitis in early infancy predicts allergic airway disease at 5 years</article-title><source>Clin Exp Allergy</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>965</fpage><lpage>970</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9756200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bergmann</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Edenharter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergmann</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Lau</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Wahn</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name></person-group><collab>the Multicenter Allergy Study Research G</collab><year>2000</year><article-title>Socioeconomic status is a risk factor for allergy in parents but not in their children</article-title><source>Clin Exp Allergy</source><volume>30</volume><fpage>1740</fpage><lpage>1745</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11122212</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Burchfiel</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Higgins</surname><given-names>MW</given-names></name><name><surname>Keller</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name><name><surname>Howatt</surname><given-names>WF</given-names></name><name><surname>Butler</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Higgins</surname><given-names>IT</given-names></name></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Passive smoking in childhood. Respiratory conditions and pulmonary function in Tecumseh, Michigan</article-title><source>Am Rev Respir Dis</source><volume>133</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>966</fpage><lpage>973</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3717768</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Rennie</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Dosman</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1996</year><article-title>Influence of environmental tobacco smoke on asthma in nonallergic and allergic children</article-title><source>Epidemiology</source><volume>7</volume><issue>5</issue><fpage>536</fpage><lpage>539</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8862988</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cook</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Strachan</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Health effects of passive smoking-10: summary of effects of parental smoking on the respiratory health of children and implications for research</article-title><source>Thorax</source><volume>54</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>357</fpage><lpage>366</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10092699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ehp0115-001394"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Daigler</surname><giv